Hi, here is the plot. Every ID has only one song session and one speech session. I would like to include the info of whether it was their first or second session (SesNum) as a between subjects factor. But since every ID has a session 01 and 02, this seems not to be legit. I could recode the variable as to whether Song was the first session or Speech was the first session (songfirst / speech first), then its a decent between subjects factor. But this is slightly different from what I actually would like to code (session 01 or 2).... I see now that this doesn't have anything to do with ezAnova itself but with me having a brain freeze on experimental design. So if you feel less inclined on following this thread, I would totally understand :)

Cheers,
Laura

